      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I\u0027m mis-understanding how this works.\n\nBefore this change it works like this\n\n1. User calls `AddBufferExpectation(buffer, expected)`\n2. a `readbackBuffer` is created and initialized to `0`\n3. a command buffer is executed to `copyBufferToBuffer(buffer, readbackBuffer)`\n4. the `readbackBuffer` and `expected` are added to some list of things\n\nAt teardown:\n\n1. all the readbackBuffers are mapped\n2. all the mapped datas is compared against expectations\n3. all the readbackBuffers are unmapped\n\nI\u0027d expect that to change to\n\n0. start recording **(added)**\n1. User calls `AddBufferExpectation(buffer, expected)`\n2. a `readbackBuffer` is created and initialized to `0` (with a unique name) **(changed)**\n3. a command buffer is executed to `copyBufferToBuffer(buffer, readbackBuffer)`\n4. the `readbackBuffer` and `expected` are added to some list of things\n5. end recording **(added)**\n\nAt teardown:\n\n0. replay recording  **(added)**\n1. all the readbackBuffers are mapped BY NAME (because they are different buffers on replay) **changed)**\n2. all the mapped datas is compared against expectations\n3. all the readbackBuffers are unmapped\n\nI don\u0027t see any reason need to `PauseRecording`... Right?",
