      "message": "As we talked in chat, I think my CL had some problems. Please let me revisit this CL and I will let you know when it\u0027s at a correct state. Sorry.\n\nlooks like why it passes the test is that: when GetObjectByLabelis called it is the same original readback buffer with the same label getting checked twice.\n\n(My original intention: For each Buffer expectation macro (ends in AddBufferExpectation) in the test body, I\u0027m adding a same buffer expectation but for the replayed one. Both the original buffer and the replayed buffer are added with a label. They are tested in the same ResolveExpectations call. So two readback buffer will be added (1 for original, 1 for replay). Capture of the readback buffer copy is paused because the replayed buffer is treated the same as the \"original test\" buffer, just 1 more expect.) (but that seems incorrect because without immediate readback the replayed buffer content could be changed when Resolving)",
